<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 45 M2, AC2.6 / D12: the master meter reads POST-master-FX, and it
  is ONE probe.

  THE OBVIOUS WIRING PRODUCES A METER THAT LOOKS BROKEN RATHER THAN WRONG.
  M2 put the master lane's chain and gain stage between the bus sum and the
  MIXER's rewire, which leaves the lane's OWN twRewire inert (T5). Both meter
  mounts call track.getRootComponent() uniformly, so a master head meter
  pointed at the lane's own rewire reads silence forever - and twLevelProbe
  answers a miss by DECAYING (proposal 34: "a page miss must DECAY the
  meter"), so the symptom is a bar that falls to nothing, which reads as a
  broken meter and not as a wiring bug.

  D12's decision is therefore to override STrack::getRootComponent() for the
  master role rather than special-case the two mounts: one answer, at the one
  place every consumer already asks.

  BUT THE SABOTAGE FOR THAT OVERRIDE DOES NOT BITE, AND THAT IS RECORDED HERE
  RATHER THAN DRESSED UP. Removing the override leaves this case GREEN. The
  reason is that the lane's own twRewire is NOT inert as D12 and T5 assume:
  STrack's constructor wires rewire.input = gainStage.output (strack.cpp), and
  wireAsMasterLane does not disconnect it - it only takes the gain stage's
  output into the MIXER's rewire as well. So the lane's rewire is REDUNDANT,
  carrying the same signal, not silent.

  The override is kept on the weaker basis that it is the one correct answer
  (the mixer's rewire genuinely is this lane's output, and it is the page cache
  the invalidation path actually bumps), not because anything here proves it
  necessary. AC2.8's "the lane's own twTrackMix and twRewire are unwired" is
  therefore NOT TRUE AS BUILT, and is open.

  WHAT THIS CASE DOES GATE is the claim in its title: the master meter reads
  post-master-FX while the TRACK meter does not. That pair fails immediately
  if the master meter is left pointing at the bus sum.

  A RENDER SITS BETWEEN THE EDIT AND THE PROBE ON PURPOSE. Levels are read
  from FROZEN PAGES BY POSITION, and proposal 34 records that stale-but-frozen
  pages are deliberately ACCEPTED - playback serves exactly those, so
  rejecting them would make the meter disagree with the ear while an edit is
  absorbed. Without the render this case would read the pre-insert page and
  assert nothing about the master chain.

  Closed forms over ../test_autosaw.wav: the meter reads 0.227598 at frame
  72000 (a shorter window than the render assertions use, hence not 0.230956),
  and 2.5x that is 0.568995.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="master_meter_postfx">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="0" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <!-- (1) With a clean master, the track meter and the master meter agree:
             the master is a unity sum of one track. -->
    <assert-meter trackPath="0"       position="72000" minRms="0.2265" maxRms="0.2287"/>
    <assert-meter trackPath="$master" position="72000" minRms="0.2265" maxRms="0.2287"/>

    <!-- (2) A 2.5x gain ON THE MASTER. -->
    <insert-plugin trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gain"
                   name="Smaragd Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0" paramId="0" value="2.5"/>
    <render filename="mmp.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>

    <!-- (3) AC2.6: the master meter is POST the master insert... -->
    <assert-meter trackPath="$master" position="72000" minRms="0.5661" maxRms="0.5718"/>

    <!-- ...and the TRACK meter is not. That pair is the assertion: a master
             meter that had simply been left pointing at the bus sum would pass
             the line above only if the two were equal, and a master meter
             reading its lane's inert rewire would have DECAYED instead. -->
    <assert-meter trackPath="0" position="72000" minRms="0.2265" maxRms="0.2287"/>

    <!-- (4) And the master fader moves it too, so the probe is downstream of
             the gain stage as well as the chain. 0.227598 x 2.5 x 0.501187 =
             0.285172. -->
    <set-track-volume trackPath="$master" volume="-6.0"/>
    <render filename="mmp6.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-meter trackPath="$master" position="72000" minRms="0.2837" maxRms="0.2866"/>
  </actions>

</SActionScript>
